judgments.prompt:
I have two implementations of the same recursive algorithm. Which one reads better to you?

Version 1:
```python
def flatten(lst):
    result = []
    for item in lst:
        if isinstance(item, list):
            result.extend(flatten(item))
        else:
            result.append(item)
    return result
```

Version 2:
```python
def flatten(lst):
    return [
        elem
        for item in lst
        for elem in (flatten(item) if isinstance(item, list) else [item])
    ]

